# freedreno: fix slot indexing in fd_set_global_binding()
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46555 state=merged
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
freedreno: fix slot indexing in fd_set_global_binding()

The loop runs i over [first, first + count), then uses first + i to
index the bindings array and i to index the caller's resources and
handles arrays. Both are off by first: the caller passes count entries
starting at index 0, and they belong in slots [first, first + count).

With first > 0 this updates the wrong bindings slots, past the end of
the array when it was only grown to first + count, and indexes
resources[] and handles[] past their end while ignoring their leading
entries.

Loop over [0, count) instead, as v3d, panfrost and asahi do in the same
dynarray-based code. rusticl, the only frontend using this hook, always
passes first = 0, so there is no functional change today.

Fixes: 5c43cf823cd ("freedreno: replace fixed array for globabl_bindings with dynamic array")
Generated-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Tupili Krishna Gowtham Reddy <tupilikr@qti.qualcomm.com>
```

